{"id": "EUVD-2026-103831", "enisaUuid": "60d99b40-2127-312a-b25b-f80d1eaedd2b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: ma35d1: Fix clock reference leak in ma35d1serial_probe()\n\nof_clk_get() returns a clock with a reference that has to be released\nwith clk_put(). ma35d1serial_probe() never does that, so the reference\nis leaked on the probe error paths and also when the port is removed.\n\nRelease it on the error paths and in ma35d1serial_remove().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3cdad0c541f899bd9a109b7dc43a1bc76123bc84", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/547c742f3b4acd4634eec47e9bff8731b55059a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8233d6b391b4cd87df6e89056c21496df7a3012", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b303d383089aae7f20ad19fee15690486b935cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98401cf912fe8a081ef8e500c421b6d957b55a99"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98746", "GHSA-74wj-7f7x-fq68"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "019e4799-f02f-3fab-a46e-fd1c65a0e56c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "930cbf92db0184e327293d5e7089be0b08d46371 <98401cf912fe8a081ef8e500c421b6d957b55a99"}, {"id": "071f80ca-19c3-36f7-a03d-53508b69e87f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "1d7ba7a8-ae0a-38da-991e-7b496e59acf6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "401c0447-943f-37d8-9a42-756322e64e6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "4c4fa125-4e6e-3e94-a679-3aaac4961b26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5683d2c6-e2e4-35e5-8c80-a67a33d6416c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ve